A '''Sextant''' is a [[currency]] item that can be used on a [[Voidstone]] to add a special modifier to [[map]]s.

==Mechanics==
Sextants are used to add a random [[enchantment]] mod to a [[Voidstone]] on the [[Atlas of Worlds]]. This effect will be applied to all non-unique maps, while only some modifiers apply to different [[unique map]]s. Voidstones can only have at most one sextant modifier on them at a time; using another sextant on that Voidstone will replace the current modifier.

Each {{il|Awakened Sextant}} mod lasts a total of three uses of maps after which it disappears. Sextant mods from [[Elevated Sextant]]s have fifteen uses. The [[Enduring Influence]] [[Atlas passive]] adds one additional use to either type of sextant when you apply one to a Voidstone; this passive can be unallocated afterwards and the remaining uses will not change.

Identical Sextant modifiers cannot be stacked. Sextants cannot roll the same mod that is already on a different Voidstone if applied while those Voidstones are socketed in the [[Atlas of Worlds]] menu. Additionally, certain types of modifiers that share a mod group (e.g. Tormented Spirits drop additional X) also cannot be stacked. If multiple non-stacking modifiers are on socketed Voidstones (e.g. via applying {{il|Charged Compass|Charged Compasses}}), only the Voidstone with higher remaining uses will consume a use.

===Storing Sextant Modifiers===

A {{il|Surveyor's Compass}} can be used on a Voidstone with a sextant modifier, removing the modifier and granting an itemized {{il|Charged Compass}} with that modifier as well as its remaining uses. This allows the sextant modifier to be traded.

